Z||000000||TOM||12-17-1999||12:41 AM||||My 86 V6 failed the smog check and I need to figure out why.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||12-17-1999||02:47 AM||||You could try moving.  Indiana is a nice place to live <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  We can always use some more Fiero talent.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ChadMan||12-17-1999||09:20 AM||||Assuming your catalytic converter is OK, the EGR system (bad solenoid or cracked tube) would be the next most likely culprit on a V6.  Does your "Service Engine Soon" light ever come on?||||reg||1
Z||000003||DJRice||12-17-1999||09:28 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/000803.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/000803.html</A> <P>This was a previous discussion on failed emissions...||||reg||1
Z||000004||mshill||12-17-1999||02:23 PM||||Tom,  I went through this in October.  I fixed everything including: fuel pump/filter, air filter, oil/filter change, distributor cap/rotor, plugs and wires.  I was failing marginally in the HC outputs.  I finally took the exhaust down and cut the cat out and found it had only a golfball size catalyst left in it.<P>I got a universal cat and an installation kit and not only passed smog, but almost didn't even register on the HC output.  In the mean time I got a good tuneup by doing all those things I should have done to begin with. <P>BTW, I am in the Sacramento, CA area.||||reg||1
Z||000005||stsmithgt||12-17-1999||04:52 PM||||Hey mine passed smog with almost a clean sweep too in Sacramento. Hmmmm go figure.||||reg||1
Z||000006||mutfish||12-17-1999||05:47 PM||||Take a good look at the convertor,the NEW one I bought from the Fiero store lasted less than 500 miles,and then the catalyst crumbled...don't know if a bunch of defective ones were made or what.Installed a so-called high flow convertor made by Catco and passed e-check with flying colors...<BR>It's a place to start anyway.....<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||william_thorniii||12-17-1999||06:29 PM||||Tom,<P>Since HC is the problem, it most likely isn't an O2 sensor, but if the cat fails...<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
Z||000008||AL||12-18-1999||12:27 AM||||hey tom,  mine faied also, so i immediately, changed the cat and o2 sensor and presto it worked.i knew it was that cause the engine was rebuilt by yours truley and the only thing i didn't change was those two things. once you change it out, tell them to make a practice run, and if it passes then do the real test. remember that after 2 failed attempts, they will label your car a gross polluter, so do the practice test first! good luck tom. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||WKDFIRO||12-18-1999||04:28 AM||||Two things (given that it is a well taken care of Fiero) can make you fail. A bad Cat or an old O2 sensor. I replaced an O2 sensor on my wife's car an hour after she failed. Drove it back and it was good to go. We have also done the same thing with a new cat. Failed, got a new cat, (the old cat had over 200,000 it HAD to GO!) when STRAIGHT to the smog guy and passed with almost no HC as well.||||reg||4
Z||000010||Monkeyman||12-18-1999||06:06 PM||||WKDFIRO-Do you dispatch trucks, mail or cops?||||reg||1
